! The Far Exclaves

''Stratum:'' High Delos constellation — ''located over other Realms''. Members of New Delos by
the morning they rose, joined to the capital by nothing but the DreamNet and shared sky.

* ''The Poseidon-coast crags'' — holy sites and random cave-bearing rocks off the Athens-region
  coast, taken by the gradient's tail. Small, scattered, mostly bare. //Prompts:// which caves
  hold anything · who visits · what the coast below thinks of its missing stones.
* ''The Artemision Exclave'' — ''the whole six miles around the Temple of Artemis near Izmir,
  raised as one piece'' — a temple district aloft over a foreign coast, the gradient's most
  distant and most deliberate-looking reach. //Prompts:// inhabited, and by whom · what the
  Temple's keepers made of the morning · why the gradient reached HERE with such precision —
  accident of holiness, or the Patroness's intent.

''Filing law:'' exclaves file here (constellation membership) and carry a locator tag toward
their host Realms; host-region worksheets may cross-reference.

